  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your 'core' cards. If you have a pair of Aces in your initial 7, never pass them, even if the other 5 cards are rubbish.\n\nThe Trash Strategy: When passing, try to give your neighbor cards that don't 'connect'. If you have a 3, 5, and 9 of different suits, those are perfect 'trash' to pass.\n\nRollout Psychology: Order your reveal strategically. If you have 3-of-a-kind, revealing those three cards first can force opponents with weaker hands to fold before they even see your last two cards.",
    Player: "Keep your 'core' cards. If you have a pair of Aces in your initial 7, never pass them, even if the other 5 cards are rubbish.\n\nThe Trash Strategy: When passing, try to give your neighbor cards that don't 'connect'. If you have a 3, 5, and 9 of different suits, those are perfect 'trash' to pass.\n\nRollout Psychology: Order your reveal strategically. If you have 3-of-a-kind, revealing those three cards first can force opponents with weaker hands to fold before they even see your last two cards.",
